<header><p class="enc-kicker"><a href="/encyclopedia/conflicts/18th-century">Conflicts &amp; Resolutions</a> · War</p><h1 class="enc-title">French invasion of Switzerland</h1><p class="enc-meta"><span class="dates">1798</span> · <a href="/centuries/18th-century">18th century</a> · Part of the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/french-revolutionary-wars">French Revolutionary Wars</a></p></header>
<div class="enc-body"><p class="enc-desc">The French invasion of <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/switzerland">Switzerland</a> took place in early 1798, when armies of the French Republic overran the Old Swiss Confederacy during the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/french-revolutionary-wars">French Revolutionary Wars</a>. Bern was defeated at Grauholz and fell in March 1798, and resistance in central Switzerland was crushed. The old confederation was replaced by the centralised <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/helvetic-republic">Helvetic Republic</a>, a French client state.</p><figure class="enc-fig"><img src="/images/encyclopedia/french-invasion-of-switzerland.jpg" alt="French invasion of Switzerland" width="320" height="235" fetchpriority="high"><figcaption>Image: Abraham Girardet · CC0 · <a href="https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/File:Entr%C3%A9e_Triomphante_des_Fran%C3%A7ais_dans_Berne,_le_25_Ventose_An_6%C3%A9me_de_la_R%C3%A9publique._G.29220_(cropped).jpg" target="_blank" rel="noopener">Wikimedia Commons</a></figcaption></figure></div>
